Dear Sir or Madam,

=20

I write further to the Court=E2=80=99s Order of 4 December 2025 and my Master

Submission for Reconsideration filed on 9 December 2025, which addressed

the Court=E2=80=99s stated concerns and set out why an oral, public permission

hearing is necessary and why determination on the papers would be unsafe.

=20

In the absence of any further direction from the Court, I proceed on the

basis that the necessity of an oral permission hearing has now been fully

pleaded and explained, and I await the Court=E2=80=99s engagement with the

Reconsideration Submission.

=20

I write also to notify the Court of material developments relevant to the

safeguarding and administrative context of the claim. The criminal

evidence referred to in the Judicial Review has now been transmitted and

placed in the public domain, and the solicitor of last record has

confirmed that they are investigating the handling and chain-of-custody

records relating to that material. No substantive information has yet

been provided as to the whereabouts or safeguarding of the evidence or

devices.

=20

These developments reinforce that the issues before the Court are live,

administrative, and continuing, and that further paper-only handling

would carry ongoing safeguarding risk.

=20

For completeness, and in light of the participation evidence already

before the Court, the Claimant respectfully notes that any oral hearing

would require appropriate participation measures, including sufficient

advance receipt of the Defendants=E2=80=99 skeleton argument (no later than

seven days prior to the hearing) to enable meaningful and effective

engagement.

=20

For the avoidance of doubt, the Claimant respectfully maintains that an

oral and public permission hearing is required and should be listed

outside the Christmas parliamentary recess (18 December 2025 to

5 January 2026), in the interests of transparency and effective public

scrutiny, and when Parliament is in session.

=20

I would be grateful for confirmation of the Court=E2=80=99s proposed next steps.

=20

Yours faithfully,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Claimant (Litigant in Person)

Judicial Review: AC-2025-LON-004293

=20

